(You hedge by buying or owning actual sugar, and "selling short" in the) Tj T*
(same amount. You sell sugar futures although you do not own any. You) Tj T*
(actually contract to deliver an amount of sugar during a specified) Tj T*
(future month at a specified price.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Eventually, you must either buy and deliver actual sugar to carry out) Tj T*
(this contract, or you must buy another contract for futures to cancel) Tj T*
(your short sale. This is known as a "covering" operation, and the) Tj T*
(cancelling of one by the other takes place automatically through the) Tj T*
(channels of the Exchange.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(From the jobber's point of view, the operation of hedging has three) Tj T*
(outstanding purposes. He may hedge:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    1. To eliminate the probability of speculative profit or loss, due) Tj T*
(    to market fluctuations.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    2. To protect a profit on a favorable purchase of actual sugar.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    3. To establish and limit a loss on an unfavorable purchase of) Tj T*
(    actual sugar.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(HEDGING _to protect a normal jobbing profit by eliminating the) Tj T*
(probability of a speculative loss or gain_.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This operation is particularly useful to jobbers with whom conditions) Tj T*
(are such that they desire to be assured that their cost will be at) Tj T*
(about the market price at the time they dispose of their sugar,) Tj T*
(regardless of whether the market be higher or lower.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Although there are times when any jobber, no matter where located, will) Tj T*
(find this a useful transaction, it is obvious that many buyers will not) Tj T*
(wish to use the market in this way unless they feel it will decline.) Tj T*
(But it is particularly of advantage to a jobber located in markets) Tj T*
(necessitating a delay of from one day to several weeks in transit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For instance, on a certain day in April, two jobbers bought their usual) Tj T*
(quantity of sugar. One was located in Syracuse, the other in New York.) Tj T*
(Two days following the purchase, the market broke half a cent per) Tj T*
(pound. In view of the fact that his sugars were still in transit when) Tj T*
(the market declined, the Syracuse buyer was obliged to sustain this) Tj T*
(entire loss, in order to meet competition. On the other hand, because) Tj T*
(he received and distributed the sugar before the market broke, the New) Tj T*
(York jobber was able not only to avoid a loss, but make his regular) Tj T*
(profit.) Tj T*
