(Point of Delivery) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Although Chicago is the delivery point in all Exchange contracts for) Tj T*
(refined sugar, it should be plainly understood that the Exchange is for) Tj T*
(anyone, anywhere. Whether located in Chicago, or in Rochester,) Tj T*
(Baltimore, New York or even San Francisco, a jobber can advantageously) Tj T*
(use the Exchange.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Deliveries of Refined Sugar Futures will be made only from the) Tj T*
(Exchange-licensed warehouses in Chicago. But, regardless of the) Tj T*
(prospective buyer's location, the delivery point is not of any material) Tj T*
(importance as it is an established fact that in operations on all) Tj T*
(exchanges the percentage of actual deliveries taken is exceptionally) Tj T*
(small. In fact, the examples used in this booklet are all based on the) Tj T*
(supposition that the buyer may find it more convenient _not_ to take) Tj T*
(delivery.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The usual procedure followed in sugar exchange operations is for the) Tj T*
(buyer to close out his exchange transaction prior to the period calling) Tj T*
(for delivery and purchasing actual sugar from the refiners, executing) Tj T*
(both transactions practically simultaneously.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Possibly the most important problem in connection with the organization) Tj T*
(of any commodity exchange is to reduce the possibility of corners,) Tj T*
(however remote, to the smallest possible degree.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
